BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:emap-emare-media-art-residencies-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261108T130143Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20261106T123000Z
DTEND:20261106T130000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 14:00 CET: EMAP / EMARE: European Media Art Platform Resid
 encies 2027
DESCRIPTION:Closes 06 Nov 2026 at 14:00 CET.\n\nThe European Media Art Plat
 form (EMAP/EMARE) is a network of leading European media-art organisations
  offering fully funded two-month production residencies for artists workin
 g with digital media\, including media art\, bio art and robotic art.\n\nO
 rganisation: European Media Art Platform (EMAP / EMARE)\nLocation: Two-mon
 th production residency at one of 15 host institutions across Austria\, Fr
 ance\, Slovakia\, Portugal\, Belgium\, Netherlands\, Slovenia\, Croatia\, 
 Spain\, Italy\, Cyprus\, Greece\, Latvia\, Germany and Poland\nAward: EUR 
 4\,000 grant for the applying artist (including subsistence)\; EUR 2\,000 
 for a collaborating artist (EUR 6\,000 total for a duo)\; EUR 4\,000 proje
 ct budget\; accommodation provided by the host\; travel covered per EU cei
 lings\; access to technical facilities and media labs. No application fee.
 \nDuration: Two months\n\nMore: https://call.emare.eu/?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://call.emare.eu/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
LOCATION:Two-month production residency at one of 15 host institutions acro
 ss Austria\, France\, Slovakia\, Portugal\, Belgium\, Netherlands\, Sloven
 ia\, Croatia\, Spain\, Italy\, Cyprus\, Greece\, Latvia\, Germany and Pola
 nd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stroom-den-haag-pro-research-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261108T130143Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stroom Den Haag: PRO Research
DESCRIPTION:Stroom Den Haag's PRO Research scheme contributes to the costs 
 of a research project or artist-in-residency that feeds the development of
  new work and benefits The Hague's art climate.\n\nOrganisation: Stroom De
 n Haag\nLocation: The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to Hague artists registere
 d with Stroom and to curators\, mediators\, critics\, publicists and other
 s professionally active in the contemporary art world\; applicants from ou
 tside The Hague apply with a CV.\nAward: Maximum EUR 5\,000 per research p
 roject\, up to EUR 20\,000 per applicant per calendar year. Amounts exclud
 e VAT and grants are only awarded on demonstrable financial need. No appli
 cation fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; the grant remains valid for up to t
 wo years after the decision meeting\, with 80 percent paid upfront and 20 
 percent on the final report\n\nMore: https://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-a
 rtists/financial-support/pro-research?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-resea
 rch?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to Hague artists registered with Str
 oom and to curators\, mediators\, critics\, publicists and others professi
 onally active in the contemporary art world\; applicants from outside The 
 Hague apply with a CV.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:art-explora-cite-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261108T130143Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: Art Explora x Cité internationale des arts Residency\, 7
 th Call (Paris)
DESCRIPTION:The 7th call of the Art Explora residency programme at the Cit
 é internationale des arts opened 21 September 2026. The programme support
 s projects exploring the crossovers of art with science\, technology and e
 cology\, which makes it one of the stronger art-science fits in Europe.\n\
 nOrganisation: Art Explora Foundation and Cité internationale des arts\nL
 ocation: Paris\, France. Open worldwide to artists with at least 5 years o
 f professional practice.\nAward: EUR 1\,000 per month living stipend plus 
 up to EUR 3\,000 production grant\, a furnished live-work studio of around
  50 m2 at the Cité internationale des arts\, round-trip travel to Paris a
 nd curatorial mentoring. No application fee.\nDuration: 3- or 6-month resi
 dencies during 2027\; 3 months for duos (artist plus researcher\, curator 
 or writer).\n\nMore: https://artexplora.plateformecandidature.com/?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://artexplora.plateformecandidature.com/?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France. Open worldwide to artists with at least 5 years of
  professional practice.
END:VEVENT
